<</Parent 28 0 R/Next 6 0 R/Prev 4 0 R/Title(I.  Nay, that I cannot do, unless you could step out of your Line altogether.)/Dest 727 0 R>>
endobj
6 0 obj
<</Parent 28 0 R/Next 7 0 R/Prev 5 0 R/Title(I.  Well, yes.  Out of YOUR World.  Out of YOUR Space.  For your Space is not the true Space.  True Space is a Plane; but your Space is only a Line.)/Dest 728 0 R>>
endobj
7 0 obj
<</Parent 28 0 R/Next 8 0 R/Prev 6 0 R/Title(I.  Pardon me, my Lord, but is not your Lordship already in Space, your Lordship and his humble servant, even at this moment?)/Dest 729 0 R>>
endobj
8 0 obj
<</Parent 28 0 R/Next 9 0 R/Prev 7 0 R/Title(I.  Space, my Lord, is height and breadth indefinitely prolonged.)/Dest 730 0 R>>
endobj
9 0 obj
<</Parent 28 0 R/Next 10 0 R/Prev 8 0 R/Title(I.  Your Lordship is pleased to be merry.  We also speak of length and height, or breadth and thickness, thus denoting Two Dimensions by four names.)/Dest 731 0 R>>
endobj
10 0 obj
<</Parent 28 0 R/Next 11 0 R/Prev 9 0 R/Title(I.  Would your Lordship indicate or explain to me in what direction is the Third Dimension, unknown to me?)/Dest 732 0 R>>
endobj
11 0 obj
<</Parent 28 0 R/Next 12 0 R/Prev 10 0 R/Title(I.  My Lord means seemingly that it is Northward and Southward.)/Dest 733 0 R>>
endobj
12 0 obj
<</Parent 28 0 R/Next 13 0 R/Prev 11 0 R/Title(I.  Pardon me, my Lord, a moment's inspection will convince your Lordship that I have a perfect luminary at the juncture of two of my sides.)/Dest 734 0 R>>
endobj
13 0 obj
